Functional Requirements (English Translation)
Registration / Login (user)

Registration / login fields: login & password

login may contain either a unique nickname or an email

password must be 8 characters or longer

Profile completion (user)

First name

Last name

City

Hobbies (from the hobbies reference list)

About me (up to 500 characters)

Nickname (if login is not an email — nickname is optional; if login is email — nickname is required)

Avatar

Creating a post with text and images

Text field: 1–1000 characters

Images: user can attach 0–1 images, size < 10 MB

A post can be deleted

Liking a post

A user can like / unlike a post (toggle) once

The like counter updates without page reload

Comments on a post

Text field: up to 500 characters

The author of a comment can delete their comment

Following a user

Actions: follow / unfollow

If a user is not following anyone, the feed is formed based on their interests specified during registration.
Otherwise — the feed is based on followed users.

The list of subscriptions is located in a separate tab: Profile → Favorites

Creating a room

Required fields:

Category (from hobbies reference list)

Date

Creation time

Title (≤ 50 characters)

Description (≤ 500 characters)

Format (online / in-person)

Type of admission (open / by request)

If online: room capacity is max 20 users

If in-person: city (default = creator’s profile city), address, unlimited participant count

The room can be published only when all required fields are filled

After publishing, the room appears in the "My Rooms" section

Room search by categories (semantic search across all room fields, ElasticSearch-like)

Indexed rooms appear in search, but full rooms do not appear in recommendation feeds.

Category filter (multiple categories selectable)

Search results contain only rooms matching selected categories

Submitting a participation request

For rooms by request:

Request form: text up to 500 characters

Request status changes (approved / rejected) trigger a notification to both the room owner and the applicant

For open rooms:

Users can join until the capacity limit is reached

Managing participation requests (room owner + moderators)

List of requests with applicant data.
Room owner + admin can approve or reject requests.

Approved users move to the participant list; reaching the limit automatically closes admission.

Room group chat

Access only for the owner and approved participants

Owner can delete messages

Owner can ban participants

One message: up to 500 characters

Images are sent as a separate message, size ≤ 10 MB

Notifications about comments / mentions

Notifications appear in the "bell" icon

A user can disable specific notifications (comments / mentions and others from notification reference list) in settings

Room notifications

Events that trigger notifications:

New request (for room owners / moderators)

Decision on a request (for applicants)

Event reminders: 1 hour / 24 hours before the event

Viewing other users’ profiles

Profile card contains:

Nickname (if present)

First name

Last name

Hobbies

Follow button

City

About the user

User rating

Room feed and sorting

Display only active rooms (rooms where:

user’s request is approved OR

the room is open)

Sorting options:

by event time (default: nearest first)

by creation date

Room card includes:

Title

Category

Date and time

Format (if in-person: city, venue)

Creator

Admission status

Occupied vs capacity

Admission may be closed manually before reaching the limit.
Reaching the limit closes admission automatically.

If the event date has passed, the room closes automatically.
Otherwise, the owner can close it manually.

Review & rating system

After event completion, participants can leave:

A review (up to 400 characters)

A rating (0–5)
For both the room and/or the mentor.

Average rating is displayed:

In the user profile

On the event page (after completion)

Additional notifications

User banned in a group

Request sent to a closed group

Acceptance into a group

User email verification status

User verification via phone number
Search posts in user profile + global post search (across the platform)
Non-Functional Requirements (NFR)
(1) Usability

Adaptive interface: supports tablets, smartphones, and laptop/PC monitors.
Other screen types are not guaranteed.

(2) Performance

SLA: API response time for key operations (feed, search, room page) — ≤ 3 seconds at 95th percentile

Chat message send/delivery — ≤ 2 seconds, messages visible after reload

Supported read load: up to 1000 rps without failures

Attachment size limits:

Posts: ≤ 10 MB

Chats: ≤ 25 MB
Bigger files are rejected.

(3) Reliability & Availability

Target service availability: 99% per month

(4) Security

Transport: HTTPS everywhere

Auth cookies: HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite=Lax

Minimum password length — 8

Error messages must not contain stack traces or internal details

RBAC: user / admin; actions outside role are forbidden

(5) Privacy

Contacts and email are hidden by default; visibility adjustable by the user

Profile data can be deleted

Data is used only for service functionality

(6) Maintainability

Documentation:

README with run instructions

Swagger / OpenAPI for REST endpoints

CI runs build, linters, and tests on every PR; build must pass successfully

(7) Scalability

Stateless components support horizontal scaling

Lists / feed support caching and pagination; heavy operations do not block UI

Real-time features (chat/notifications) via persistent connections (WebSocket / SSE)

Features

Social network: post creation with “rooms” integration, likes, dislikes, views, etc.

User verification

Ability to attach external links: personal website, GitHub

Subscriptions + feed + notification bell

Ready-made presets (“Basketball”, “Java Partner”) and the ability to duplicate them with a new date

Open rooms = one-click join; request-based rooms = short form; chat supports file attachments

Event reminders: 24h and 1h before the event

After the event: participants leave rating + review; verified mentors / creators get visible badges

Interest-based recommendations & Similar rooms

Social feed of posts